    "body": "I tested the remaining pocket blocks on our iTNC 530 programming station (`606425 004 SP20`). I split the original file at `N590`, where the tool retracts after the first depth pass. Both files fit within the demo limit.\n\n- Pass 1 kept the original header through `N590`, then used the original shutdown blocks from `N1120` through the footer.\n- Pass 2 kept the original header through `N70`, then used `N600` through the footer. This preserved the move from `N990` to `N1000` and every remaining block.\n\nThe station returned all 64 lines of each file unchanged. Both Test Runs reached `STOP REASON: block END PGM or M02` without a numbered alarm in the run log. Together the two runs covered every original block, including `N1000` through `N1140`. The graphics pane stayed blank and displayed `ERROR` in both runs, so stock removal remains unverified.\n\nThe original 116-line file still awaits a continuous run. I can test it later on the physical Fehlmann Picomax 55, which runs `340490-03`.\n",
