    "body": "I tested files 1 to 3 on our iTNC 530 programming station. It runs NC software `606425 004 SP20`. I used the original bytes from your comment (main `edcbfe4dd`). The line counts matched: 17, 22 and 22. I loaded each file as `VMC_3-AXIS.I` in its own folder.\n\n| Program | Question | Station result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `drill_peck` | Does `N100 G205` load and run now? | Yes. The control accepted `N100 G205` with `Q208=+99999.999`. All 17 lines matched on readback, with no `ERROR =` block. Test Run reached `STOP REASON: block END PGM or M02`. |\n| `drill_plate` | Do both Cycle 200 blocks load and run? | Yes. All 22 lines matched on readback, `N100 G200` and `N150 G200` included. Test Run reached the same program end. |\n| `ream` | Does the control accept `G247 Q339=1`? | Yes. All 22 lines matched on readback. The control wrote `N20 G247 Q339=+1`. This differs from the input only by the `+` sign. Test Run reached the same program end. |\n\nThe Test Run logs recorded no numbered alarm and no `ERROR SOURCE` line for the three runs.\n\nNot verified: the graphics pane stayed blank and showed `ERROR` in all three runs. Stock removal and the drilled depth are therefore unverified. This is the same as in my first tests.\n\nFile 4 (the 276-block pocket) is not tested. It needs a run on the physical Fehlmann Picomax 55 (`340490-03`). That run follows later this week.\n",
